                              Review by mitchellh                               

Summary                                                                         

There's good stuff here. Params is the right shape, the state machine and the   
stream fast path sharing one accumulator is something I've wanted for awhile,   
and I've been saying we'd add a heap slow path for params "one day" since the 24
limit went in. Appreciate the disclosure and that you explained your own        
reasoning too.                                                                  

Two things before I'd vouch:                                                    

 1 This is front-running the multi-cursor protocol. GroupIterator isn't used by 
   anything in this PR and the > q case in allowsSubparams is for a sequence we 
   don't handle anywhere yet. Drop both and bring them with the cursors PR. I   
   don't want to land an allowlist entry for something we don't parse, and if   
   that PR changes shape this becomes dead code nobody remembers.               
 2 This is the hottest path in the parser. push went from an inline array store 
   to a function call with a handful of branches per separator, and that's in   
   both the state machine and the stream loop. Did you benchmark this? Please   
   post stream bench numbers before/after. I've been burned by icache here      
   before, that's literally why the warn functions are noinline.                

The 256 thing is fine, the bit set needs a bound anyway so that's a good enough 
reason.                                                                         

Once those are sorted I'd probably tag this for 1.4 and let it bake in tip for a
bit since it touches every CSI we parse.                                        

Inline Comments                                                                 

